=== elfedit ===
DESCRIPTION ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Update the ELF header of ELF files

Report bugs to <https://sourceware.org/bugzilla/>


USAGE ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  elfedit <option(s)> elffile(s)


POSITIONALS (1) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  elffile(s)


FLAGS (12) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The options are
--input-mach [{…}]
    Set input machine type
      values: none, i386, iamcu, l1om, k1om, x86_64
--output-mach [{…}]
    Set output machine type
      values: none, i386, iamcu, l1om, k1om, x86_64
--input-type [{…}]
    Set input file type
      values: none, rel, exec, dyn
--output-type [{…}]
    Set output file type
      values: none, rel, exec, dyn
--input-osabi
  [none|HPUX|NetBSD|GNU|Linux|Solaris|AIX|Irix|FreeBSD|TRU64|Modesto|OpenBSD
  |OpenVMS|NSK|AROS|FenixOS]
    Set input OSABI
--output-osabi
  [none|HPUX|NetBSD|GNU|Linux|Solaris|AIX|Irix|FreeBSD|TRU64|Modesto|OpenBSD
  |OpenVMS|NSK|AROS|FenixOS]
    Set output OSABI
--input-abiversion [0-255]
    Set input ABIVERSION
--output-abiversion [0-255]
    Set output ABIVERSION
--enable-x86-feature [{…}]
    Enable x86 feature
      values: ibt, shstk, lam_u48, lam_u57
--disable-x86-feature [{…}]
    Disable x86 feature
      values: ibt, shstk, lam_u48, lam_u57
-h, --help
    Display this information
-v, --version
    Display the version number of elfedit
